    "title": "Fort Wayne FC shuts out Richmond Kickers 2-0, jumping back into playoff position - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Josh Ayen ,\n1 hours ago\nFORT WAYNE, Ind. (WANE) - Fort Wayne FC is back in playoff position nearly two-thirds of the way through the USL League One regular season following a 2-0 win over last-place Richmond Kickers on Wednesday.\nAfter stumbling through four straight losses, including five losses in six matches, Fort Wayne has bounced back with two consecutive wins.\nScoreless through most of the first half, Fort Wayne broke the deadlock just before halftime. Jaydon Smith followed through on a shot attempt from Javier Armas to put Fort Wayne ahead 1-0 at the break. Jack Thomas knocked in an insurance goal on a set piece off a pass from Michael Rempel in the 75th minute.\nMeanwhile, Bernd Schipmann earned his eighth clean sheet of the season after Fort Wayne allowed five total shots to Richmond. Only one of Richmond's attempts was on frame.\nFort Wayne FC (9-7-6) looks to keep rolling on Saturday against New York Cosmos. Kickoff is scheduled for 7:30 p.m. at Ruoff Mortgage Stadium.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WANE 15.",
    "summary": "(WANE) - Fort Wayne FC is back in playoff position nearly two-thirds of the way through the USL League One regular season following a 2-0 win over last-place Richmond Kickers on Wednesday. Jaydon Smith followed through on a shot attempt from Javier Armas to put Fort Wayne ahead 1-0 at the break. Jack Thomas knocked in an insurance goal on a set piece off a pass from Michael Rempel in the 75th minute. Meanwhile, Bernd Schipmann earned his eighth clean sheet of the season after Fort Wayne allowed five total shots to Richmond.",
